      "content": "GENERAL information",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "d2ed7145-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "This agreement is subject to revision without prior notice. Please check with a counselor every semester to obtain current information about possible changes in the agreement. To learn more about the courses and programs offered at Sonoma State University or the General Education and Upper-division requirements for each major please refer to the university catalog at: http://www.sonoma.edu/catalog/",
      "contentHtml": "This agreement is subject to revision without prior notice.  Please check with a counselor every semester to obtain current information about possible changes in the agreement.  To learn more about the courses and programs offered at Sonoma State University or the General Education and Upper-division requirements for each major please refer to the university catalog at: <a href=\"http://www.sonoma.edu/catalog/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sonoma.edu/catalog/</a>"
    },
    {
      "id": "97bd7645-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "IMPORTANT TRANSFER INFORMATION",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "c0337445-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "To be admitted to the English major, students must receive a grade of at least B- in ENGL 101 and 214 or their equivalents. Students with a grade lower than B- in either ENGL 101 or 214 may petition for a review by the department. All single subject concentration courses must be passed with a grade of C or better in order to qualify as meeting the waiver requirements. In addition, students must achieve a minimum GPA of 3.00 (in single subject program courses) to qualify for waiver approval. ENGLISH EDUCATION CONCENTRATION total of 52 units in the English Education concentration is required.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>To be admitted to the English major, students must receive a grade of at least B- in ENGL 101 and 214 or their equivalents. Students with a grade lower than B- in either ENGL 101 or 214 may petition for a review by the department. All single subject concentration courses must be passed with a grade of C or better in order to qualify as meeting the waiver requirements. In addition, students must achieve a minimum GPA of 3.00 (in single subject program courses) to qualify for waiver approval. </p><p><br></p><p>ENGLISH EDUCATION CONCENTRATION total of 52 units in the English Education concentration is required.</p>"
    }
  ],
